Z||000007||My7Fieros||06-02-2000||03:31 AM||||Hi I had the same prob.(headlights) w/one of my 88's. Not to take anything away from anyone, but, the 87/88 motors are EASY to rebuild! Take em out, pull out the motors (super easy) and take out the 3 bolts on the side of the motor (1/4 socket). More than likely a powdery white substance will come out. Clean it out, then get glue sticks (yes, glue sticks)from a hardware store or one of those Martha Stewart type places. Cut the stick to the appropriate length (around1/2 in or so) and put them in the 3 lobes in the white wheel. Reassemble and install and watch em work like new! Whole process to me about 20 minutes. Just dont use coathanger wires or bricks to hold your lights up! ha ha||||reg||1
